FV2021 Coleopteran (40 MP)
--------------------------

A humanoid walker three metres tall, built in Britain and fielded
by Canada's forces on Mars.  Its pilot wears a “thought-linked”
helmet, and the link is what makes it so nimble.  The helmet is
tuned to one pilot's brain — a new pilot must wait a day while it
is retuned; until then, halve the Defence Mastery and Combat
Technique: Lightning Reflexes Attribute bonuses.  The paint is the
usual UN scheme, white with sky-blue heads.


**Derived Values** — AR 20, HP 80

**Mecha Sub-Attributes** — 
**Accessories — Level 2** (Radio, Inertial Navigation. 2 MP), **Ground Speed — Level 1** (Up to 50 kph. 2 MP), **Heavy Armour — Level 2** (Partial, thin. 7 MP), **Life Support — Level 2** (2 MP), **Manoeuvre Bonus — Level 4** (Ground only; +2 to Initiative and +2 to Defense Combat Value. 4 MP), **Sensors — Level 1** (Range to 10 kilometres (1,000 km in space). 1 MP), **Super-Strength — Level 1** (3 MP), **Toughness — Level 2** (+40 Health Points. 8 MP), **Weapon: Plasma Fist — Level 2** (Damage ACV+75, Melee, Limited Shots: 6 shots. 1 MP), **Weapon: Railgun — Level 3** (Damage ACV+45, Long-Range: 5 km, Unreliable. 12 MP), **Weapon: Rocket Pod — Level 2** (Damage ACV+15, Auto-fire, Area Effect, Limited Shots ×2: 3 shots,
Stoppable. 1 MP)

**Mecha Defects** — 
**Awkward Size** (Large: 1-10 tonnes. 2 MBP), **Hanger Queen** (1 MBP)

**Notes:**

- Punch: Damage ACV+10, Muscle-Powered, Melee

